## Methodology

Soil moisture is expressed as a percentile rank (0–1) from the AWRA-L v7 decile product, calibrated against the full 1911–present historical record for each location and season. A composite stress index combines soil moisture deficit (60% weight), vapour pressure deficit (25%), and maximum temperature (15%), normalised against agronomic critical thresholds (40 °C; 3.2 kPa VPD). Risk levels are assigned from the stress index: Critical ≥ 0.85, Alert 0.60–0.85, Watch 0.35–0.60, Low < 0.35. This product describes conditions relative to historical norms — it is not a forecast of future rainfall and does not constitute a formal drought declaration.

## Caveats

- Grid-cell resolution is 0.05° (~5 km). Conditions at individual paddock or property scale may differ materially.
- Soil moisture reflects the AWRA-L model estimate, not direct field measurement.
- Temperature and VPD are averaged over the selected period; short-duration heatwave events within the period may be damped.
- This bulletin is for situational awareness only. Formal drought declarations follow separate DPIRD processes.

